       FontWeight->"Bold"], "::", "usage"}], "=", 
     "\"\<ExCDFRSSEven[p1, p2, p22, x, prec] computes the value for the exact \
CDF or p-value for the partial Lambda for the random sample size case for any \
of the sampling distributions in the paper, for even p1 or even p22;\n\
arguments are (in this order):\n\!\(\*StyleBox[\"p1\",FontWeight->\"Bold\"]\) \
- the number of variables of the 1st set\n\
\!\(\*StyleBox[\"p2\",FontWeight->\"Bold\"]\) - the number of variables of \
the 2nd set\np22 - the number of variables in X2 that were taken out in the \
submodel \n\!\(\*StyleBox[\"x\",FontWeight->\"Bold\"]\) - the value of Lambda \
for which we want to compute the CDF or p-value\n\
\!\(\*StyleBox[\"prec\",FontWeight->\"Bold\"]\) - an optional argument \
setting the number of precision digits for the computation of the GNIG CDF \
(default value: 150)\>\""}], ";"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
